# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Avatar 30 fps source, no frame generation, -src 30, b:vsync present, -lock -lag 75 -mark -etw -dejit, 2026-09-16: one benchmark test, no fade at either end, opened 2.3 s after the fade ends so the window starts once the benchmark is fully running, the same margin the 60x2 steady row uses. The 2:1 case on the copy-free capture loop with the re-engage window live: strict alternation of one real frame and one w=0.5 midpoint blend, lock engaged on every present.
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Avatar 30 fps source, no frame generation, -src 30, b:vsync present, -lock -lag 75 -mark -etw -dejit, 2026-09-16: one benchmark test, no fade at either end, opened 2.3 s after the fade ends so the window starts once the benchmark is fully running, the same margin the 60x2 steady row uses. The 2:1 case on the copy-free capture loop with the re-engage window live: strict alternation of one real frame and one w=0.5 midpoint blend, lock engaged on every present.
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 1
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 50.0
src_hint 30.0
# Replay 50.0% / worst 1 against field 50.0% / worst 1 over 1651 presents: exact. The 2:1 case
# doing the lock's real work, one real frame alternating with one w=0.5 midpoint blend for the
# whole test. max_worst_run 1 is the alternation itself: two blends in a row means the pull
# stopped holding the comb, and no bound here can be loosened without saying which break is
# acceptable. The window opens once the benchmark is fully running, like the 60x2 steady row;
# the shorter margin the other fixtures use replays the same here, and the margin is kept
# uniform so a future policy change cannot fail this row for a cold-start reason.
max_worst_run 1
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 50.4
min_reseeds 0
